Content shell: the system's file chooser for <input type=file>.

The shell's desktop platforms answered every file chooser by cancelling it,
so a click on <input type=file> did nothing and a folder dropped on an
<input webkitdirectory> was refused. They now do what Chrome does: the
system's dialog (the XDG desktop portal on Linux, NSOpenPanel on macOS, the
common dialog on Windows), with the input's accept types as filters, one
file or many, or a folder listed recursively; a dropped folder is listed
the same way. ShellFileSelectHelper, which the shell built only for iOS,
does it everywhere now. A CDP client that intercepts file choosers
(Page.setInterceptFileChooserDialog) still gets them first, from content.

